{
  "requirement": "Every {term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain` implements\n`trust_but_verify::domain::Domain`. A domain is cloneable and safe to share between\nexecutions. The following chapters introduce its members one capability at a\ntime.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    type Error: Send;\n    type NodeData: Clone + Eq + Hash + Send + Sync;\n    type NodeContent: NodeContents;\n    type EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync;\n\n    fn cache(&self) -> &ValidationCache<Self>;\n    fn node_path(&self, node: &NodeId<Self>) -> NodePath;\n    fn node_content(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeContent, Self::Error>;\n    fn outgoing_edges(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n        label: Self::EdgeLabel,\n    ) -> Result<Vec<NodeId<Self>>, Self::Error>;\n    fn load_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Option<Record<Self::NodeData, Self::EdgeLabel>>, Self::Error>> + Send;\n    fn store_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n        record: &Record<Self::NodeData, Self::EdgeLabel>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), Self::Error>> + Send;\n\n    fn project_sources(&self) -> Option<SourceProject<Self>> { ... }\n    fn source_node(\n        &self,\n        item: &OutlineData,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeData, SourceError> { ... }\n    fn source_address(&self, _data: &Self::NodeData) -> Option<OutlineData> { ... }\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.domain`. I derived these obligations from its text:\n\n1. Every application domain implements `Domain`.\n2. A domain is `Clone + Send + Sync`.\n3. A domain can be shared between executions.\n4. The associated types carry these bounds:\n   - `Error: Send`.\n   - `NodeData: Clone + Eq + Hash + Send + Sync`.\n   - `NodeContent: NodeContents`.\n   - `EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync`.\n5. The required methods `cache`, `node_path`, `node_content`, `outgoing_edges`, `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` exist with the declared signatures. The two evidence futures are `Send`.\n6. The default methods `project_sources`, `source_node` and `source_address` exist and have sensible defaults.\n\nHow the tests cover them:\n\n- **Bounds.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` defines an opaque `Relationships` domain. Its `GraphError` holds a `Cell`, so it is `Send` but not `Sync`. Its `Identity` and `Label` types are also opaque. The nested generic `check_bounds<G: Domain>` is compiled against the declared bounds:\n  - `domain::<G>()` requires `Clone + Send + Sync` on the domain.\n  - `identity` requires `Clone + Eq + Hash + Send + Sync` on `NodeData`.\n  - `label` requires `Clone + Send + Sync` on `EdgeLabel`.\n  - `error` requires only `Send` on `Error`.\n  - `contents` requires `NodeContents + Send + Sync` on `NodeContent`.\n  - `send(graph.load_evidence(..))` and `send(graph.store_evidence(..))` check that the evidence futures are `Send`.\n  - A bound that is loosened or too strict would fail to compile.\n- **Required methods.** The same test asserts the outcomes of the required methods:\n  - `node_content` returns `format` \"1\" and a fingerprint value of \"1\".\n  - `load_evidence` returns `None` and `store_evidence` returns `Ok`.\n  - `node_path` returns `[\"relationships\", \"1\"]` and differs between nodes.\n  - `outgoing_edges` returns the expected lists for several labels, including an empty list.\n  - `outgoing_edges` returns an error for an unknown node, and that error is checked as `Send`.\n- **Default methods.** `domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors` asserts that `project_sources()` is `None` and that `source_node` returns `SourceError::Invalid`. `domain_without_project_sources_leaves_source_tools_disabled` asserts the same for `Application`. It also asserts that `source_address` is `None`. The case where a domain does supply project sources belongs to the sources requirements, not to this one.\n- **Application domains implement the trait.** The `Application` and `Relationships` fixtures implement `Domain`. The `public_exports_match_the_appendix` test (`crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs`) also compiles the shipping Habeas consumer against the SDK.\n- **Sharing between executions.** The concurrent tests run executions against one shared domain, each with its own context or validator: `concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records`, `concurrent_single_node_validations_keep_separate_traces`, `shared_context_allows_independent_concurrent_agent_calls` and `concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads`. They assert that each execution's records and traces stay isolated.\n- **Typical use.** `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent`, `behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer` and `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` show the trait's methods used together through validation, storage and reload.\n\nI found no untested obligation. I also found no marking gap.",
  "references": "1219af9c261c7c256deaf030045562c41b04d884087245d89e34d2f09aa8f735",
